          "quote": "Let $p\\ge1$, let $\\mathcal X$ be a finite nonempty candidate set, and let $f_x\\in\\mathbb R^p$ be the feature vector for each $x\\in\\mathcal X$. An approximate design $\\xi$ and information matrix $M(\\xi)=\\sum_x\\xi_xf_xf_x^T$ use the convention of [[def-approximate-linear-model-design-and-optimality-criteria]]. The same vectors may be scalar-observation sensitivities at a fixed parameter, as in [[def-nonlinear-experimental-design-and-local-identifiability]], with a scalar precision absorbed into $f_x$. The procedure uses exact arithmetic.\n\n**Input:** A finite nonempty $\\mathcal X$, $p\\ge1$, its feature vectors $(f_x)_{x\\in\\mathcal X}$, an approximate initial design $\\xi^{(0)}$, and a finite nonnegative integer budget $N$ counting weight updates.\n\n**Procedure:** Form $M_0=M(\\xi^{(0)})$. If $M_0$ is not positive definite, return $(\\xi^{(0)},\\text{undefined violation},\\text{invalid initial design})$. Otherwise, for $k=0,1,\\ldots,N$, with current $\\xi^{(k)}$ and $M_k=M(\\xi^{(k)})$, compute\n$$s_x^{(k)}=f_x^TM_k^{-1}f_x\\quad(x\\in\\mathcal X),\\qquad v_k=\\max_{x\\in\\mathcal X}s_x^{(k)}-p.$$\nIf $v_k=0$, return $(\\xi^{(k)},v_k,\\text{equivalence-certified})$. If $k=N$, return $(\\xi^{(k)},v_k,\\text{budget-exhausted})$. Otherwise set\n$$\\xi_x^{(k+1)}=\\xi_x^{(k)}\\frac{s_x^{(k)}}p\\quad(x\\in\\mathcal X),$$\nform $M_{k+1}=\\sum_x\\xi_x^{(k+1)}f_xf_x^T$, and continue. The proved update invariant keeps every later $M_k$ positive definite.\n\nThe budget guarantees at most $N$ updates and $N+1$ sensitivity scans. A nonzero returned violation is reported as-is; it is not an exact D-optimality certificate. The exact integer allocation problem remains separate from this approximate-weight procedure.\n",
